# Homebrew formula template for the `jongtae/agentos` tap.
#
# The published formula does NOT live in this repository -- the tap
# `Jongtae/homebrew-agentos` is Formula-only by an explicit earlier migration
# decision (docs/issue-branch-ledger.jsonl, first record). That is why
# `git ls-files` finds no `.rb` here, and why "no formula exists" is the wrong
# reading of that absence: a live tap exists and is what `brew install
# jongtae/agentos/agentos` resolves.
#
# This template exists so the relationship is traceable FROM this repository.
# Before it, the only links were a prose URL in QUICKSTART.md and a Python
# default in src/personal_agent/delivery.py.
#
# THIS FILE IS A REFERENCE COPY, NOT A RENDER SOURCE. Nothing reads it.
# The release path (`delivery.py:406-408`) clones the tap and rewrites the two
# lines of the *existing* Formula/agentos.rb with two `re.sub` calls. Do not
# paste this file into the tap: this header describes in-repo test invariants
# that are false and meaningless once published.
#
# Because nothing reads it, it can drift from the published formula while this
# repository's suite stays green. If the tap formula changes structurally,
# re-sync this file in the same release. That obligation is written down in
# docs/release.en.md step 7 and is not automated.
#
# The two placeholders below mark what the release path substitutes, and are
# only knowable after the tag is pushed, because the archive they describe
# does not exist until then:
#
#   __VERSION__  the release version, matching pyproject.toml, without the `v`
#   __SHA256__   sha256 of the GitHub-generated tag archive
#
# `__SHA256__` is deliberately NOT a plausible-looking hex string. A formula
# carrying a fabricated checksum would install nothing and would look valid in
# review; tests/test_release_traceability.py asserts this slot stays a
# placeholder. GitHub's tarball is not byte-reproducible from a local
# `git archive`, so this value cannot honestly be precomputed here.
#
# See docs/release.en.md for the full procedure.

class Agentos < Formula
  desc "Self-hosted personal agent with browser setup and Telegram"
  homepage "https://github.com/Jongtae/agentos"
  url "https://github.com/Jongtae/agentos/archive/refs/tags/v__VERSION__.tar.gz"
  sha256 "__SHA256__"
  depends_on "python@3.13"

  def install
    system Formula["python@3.13"].opt_bin/"python3.13", "-m", "venv", libexec
    system libexec/"bin/pip", "install", buildpath
    (bin/"agentos").write <<~PYTHON
      #!#{libexec}/bin/python
      from personal_agent.quickstart import main
      main()
    PYTHON
  end

  def caveats
    <<~EOS
      Run agentos start to open browser setup.
      Data: ~/.local/share/agentos
      Keep the process running to receive Telegram requests.
    EOS
  end

  test do
    assert_match "personal agent", shell_output("#{bin}/agentos --help")
  end
end
